You are editing a learner-facing Databricks notebook (`.py` source format)
in a numbered module folder.

Follow the **Required reads** in
@docs/standards/notebook-authoring-checklist.md before writing or editing any
cell. If the active command is `/new-lesson`, or the notebook is still a
scaffold with `TODO` placeholders and without full prose sections, apply the
checklist's **Scaffold bar**. Otherwise, apply its **Full-lesson bar**. The
checklist is the single source of truth for both bar definitions; do not
re-enumerate them here.

For a full lesson from a skeleton, the author should use `/write-lesson`
(not ad-hoc chat) so every standard loads consistently. After writing,
`/validate-notebook` is the authoring-quality gate.

Do not duplicate the content of those files here — they are the canonical
source. If something in a notebook conflicts with them, follow the
standards files and the module README's notebook plan.

Automatic-write restrictions are owned by the **Do not write automatically**
section in @AGENTS.md.
